WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.932
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:08.990
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:14.740
Unit two: School Life. Today you will talk about school experiences using the present perfect.

4
00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.844
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.230
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:24.003
Curriculum.

7
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:28.142
Curriculum means all the subjects taught at a school.

8
00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:31.353
Our curriculum includes English and IT.

9
00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.324
Your turn. Say: Curriculum.

10
00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.086
Curriculum.

11
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.165
Extracurricular.

12
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.194
Extracurricular means done outside normal lessons.

13
00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:47.154
Debate is an extracurricular activity.

14
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.902
Your turn. Say: Extracurricular.

15
00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.116
Extracurricular.

16
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:56.828
Principal.

17
00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:00.176
Principal means the head teacher of a school.

18
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:02.899
The principal gave us certificates.

19
00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:05.799
Your turn. Say: Principal.

20
00:01:08.633 --> 00:01:09.518
Principal.

21
00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:11.308
Detention.

22
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:15.918
Detention means a punishment of staying at school after class.

23
00:01:16.517 --> 00:01:18.307
He got detention for being late.

24
00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:21.499
Your turn. Say: Detention.

25
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:25.218
Detention.

26
00:01:25.983 --> 00:01:27.042
Assembly.

27
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.572
Assembly means a meeting of the whole school.

28
00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:33.380
We sing the national anthem at assembly.

29
00:01:33.983 --> 00:01:36.578
Your turn. Say: Assembly.

30
00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:40.539
Assembly.

31
00:01:41.283 --> 00:01:42.447
Peer pressure.

32
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.576
Peer pressure means the feeling that you must do what your friends do.

33
00:01:47.183 --> 00:01:48.927
Don't give in to peer pressure.

34
00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:52.239
Your turn. Say: Peer pressure.

35
00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.252
Peer pressure.

36
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:57.774
Bullying.

37
00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:01.909
Bullying means hurting or scaring someone again and again.

38
00:02:02.517 --> 00:02:04.296
Our school says no to bullying.

39
00:02:04.883 --> 00:02:07.420
Your turn. Say: Bullying.

40
00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:11.140
Bullying.

41
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:13.233
Report card.

42
00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:17.505
Report card means a paper that shows your grades.

43
00:02:18.117 --> 00:02:20.488
My report card has improved this term.

44
00:02:21.083 --> 00:02:24.293
Your turn. Say: Report card.

45
00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:28.494
Report card.

46
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.402
Semester.

47
00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:33.672
Semester means one half of the school year.

48
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:36.492
The second semester starts in March.

49
00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:39.562
Your turn. Say: Semester.

50
00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.215
Semester.

51
00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:44.742
Club.

52
00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.435
Club means a group of people who meet for an activity.

53
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.817
I have joined the science club.

54
00:02:51.417 --> 00:02:53.512
Your turn. Say: Club.

55
00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.066
Club.

56
00:02:57.817 --> 00:02:58.922
Scholarship.

57
00:02:59.917 --> 00:03:03.112
Scholarship means money given to a good student to study.

58
00:03:03.717 --> 00:03:06.088
She has won a scholarship to study abroad.

59
00:03:06.683 --> 00:03:09.196
Your turn. Say: Scholarship.

60
00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.360
Scholarship.

61
00:03:14.117 --> 00:03:15.002
Achievement.

62
00:03:16.017 --> 00:03:18.736
Achievement means something good you did with effort.

63
00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:21.442
Winning the quiz was a big achievement.

64
00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.273
Your turn. Say: Achievement.

65
00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:28.111
Achievement.

66
00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.423
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:33.283 --> 00:03:36.119
Visal, have you joined any clubs this semester?

68
00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.669
Yes, I have joined the English debate club.

69
00:03:40.783 --> 00:03:43.331
Great! Have you won any competitions?

70
00:03:44.417 --> 00:03:48.796
Not yet, but my friend Sophea has won a scholarship!

71
00:03:49.883 --> 00:03:52.396
Wonderful. Has the club helped you?

72
00:03:53.483 --> 00:03:59.317
Yes! My confidence has grown, and my report card has improved.

73
00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.897
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.748
Grammar focus: Present perfect for experience.

75
00:04:06.048 --> 00:04:07.165
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.246
I have joined a club.

77
00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.790
She has won a scholarship.

78
00:04:12.683 --> 00:04:14.497
Have you ever been in detention?

79
00:04:15.433 --> 00:04:19.627
Use the present perfect for experiences when the exact time is not important.

80
00:04:20.383 --> 00:04:24.092
Be careful! Don't say: I have join a club.

81
00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:28.126
Say: I have joined a club.

82
00:04:28.426 --> 00:04:31.551
After have or has, use the past participle.

83
00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:35.286
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.856
My Extracurricular Club.

85
00:04:38.156 --> 00:04:41.479
Our principal spoke at assembly about peer pressure and bullying.

86
00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.664
She said we should be kind and join a club.

87
00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.340
This semester, I have joined the school drama club.

88
00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:52.308
It has improved my report card and my confidence.

89
00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.835
Two members have won scholarships. That is a great achievement!

90
00:04:57.933 --> 00:05:02.249
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:03.083 --> 00:05:04.827
She blank won a scholarship.

92
00:05:05.127 --> 00:05:08.131
A, has. B, have. C, is.

93
00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.376
The answer is A: has.

94
00:05:14.517 --> 00:05:16.806
The head teacher of a school is the blank.

95
00:05:17.106 --> 00:05:20.702
A, principal. B, semester. C, club.

96
00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:26.940
The answer is A: principal.

97
00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:30.269
One half of the school year is a blank.

98
00:05:30.569 --> 00:05:34.280
A, semester. B, curriculum. C, detention.

99
00:05:37.833 --> 00:05:40.019
The answer is A: semester.

100
00:05:41.233 --> 00:05:44.768
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:45.617 --> 00:05:49.694
Describe an extracurricular activity you enjoy at school.

102
00:05:58.483 --> 00:05:59.926
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:08.186
I enjoy the English club. I have made new friends there, and I have given two speeches. It has really improved my confidence.

104
00:06:08.486 --> 00:06:10.335
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:16.294
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and present perfect for experience.

106
00:06:16.594 --> 00:06:20.152
Today's value is courage. Try new things and be brave.

107
00:06:20.452 --> 00:06:22.802
See you in Unit three. Goodbye!

108
00:06:23.102 --> 00:06:26.045
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

